Reproduce and extend a full process-industry supply optimisation study (@cs-network-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Enterprise-wide-Optimization-Grossmann.lingua#r_4XD1X5QN83H40RBMGJVSZY9Y8V", #source "../sources/Process-Industry-Supply-Chain-Management-Liu.lingua#r_5W74Q34MKEJAWVS30JV4QH01YQ", #source "../sources/Graduate-Logistics-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_4NMCCS7JPNK6CD9V9Z4XTQPKR8", #source "../sources/Graduate-Supply-Chain-Planning-MIT.lingua#r_16MZ0PJM4KC10A3D9AYYESBT6P", #source "../sources/Fundamentals-of-Supply-Chain-Theory-Snyder-Shen.lingua#r_4MFFYSAE67RQNHCV2AAQ1X0GXJ", #chemical-supply-systems "A-complete-qualified-chemical-supply-system.lingua#r_44MR9J6NH9MF50YCHKGAT4GMK3") { r_7YE7Q92PG3WT8Y743XF05AX74B
**Read:** [Enterprise-wide Optimization: A New Frontier in Process Systems Engineering — Grossmann](../sources/Enterprise-wide-Optimization-Grossmann.lingua#r_4XD1X5QN83H40RBMGJVSZY9Y8V), the whole paper and full selected primary references; [Supply chain management for the process industry — Songsong Liu](../sources/Process-Industry-Supply-Chain-Management-Liu.lingua#r_5W74Q34MKEJAWVS30JV4QH01YQ), the entire thesis and selected underlying model papers/data; [Graduate Logistics Systems — MIT ESD.260J](../sources/Graduate-Logistics-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_4NMCCS7JPNK6CD9V9Z4XTQPKR8), the complete public graduate programme; [Graduate Supply Chain Planning — MIT 15.762J](../sources/Graduate-Supply-Chain-Planning-MIT.lingua#r_16MZ0PJM4KC10A3D9AYYESBT6P), the complete public graduate programme; [Fundamentals of Supply Chain Theory — Snyder and Shen](../sources/Fundamentals-of-Supply-Chain-Theory-Snyder-Shen.lingua#r_4MFFYSAE67RQNHCV2AAQ1X0GXJ), the whole authorized book as an optional theoretical extension.

Read Grossmann's complete perspective and Liu's whole doctoral thesis, then obtain the full primary formulations, data and corrections for a chosen model. Complete both public graduate programmes and the mathematical background needed for the methods. Snyder/Shen offers an optional whole-book route to deeper theory; use authorized access and identify any missing source material.

Reproduce a small published case before extending it. Derive all conservation, capacity, time, sequence/changeover, inventory and acceptance constraints, as well as the objective and uncertainty representation. Record units, variable domains, physical meanings and evidence for parameters. Compare the published result using an independent method, bound, reformulation or exact small case.

Extend the question toward actual chemical supply: multiple grades, contact/qualification restrictions, release delays, common dependencies, returns/recovery or a different service objective. Compare deterministic, scenario-based and other justified approaches using full primary methods. Report feasibility, optimality/bounds, scaling, solver settings, sensitivity and computational limits.

Defend a substantial reproducible research report through alternative formulations, competing objectives and independent critique, then revise it. Separate a mathematically feasible solution from actual available facilities/contracts and demonstrated operations. The scholarly result should deepen understanding of a supply decision and its physical consequences, with uncertain or missing data visible rather than hidden behind a solver's success message.

**Continue:** [Defend one complete chemical supply from origin to use and recovery](A-complete-qualified-chemical-supply-system.lingua#r_44MR9J6NH9MF50YCHKGAT4GMK3).

